.TH rev-stealth-config-edit 1  "rev-stealth-config-edit " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-edit \- P6.3: Open the target file in `$EDITOR` (falling back to `vi`). On editor exit, the candidate is validated. If validation succeeds the file is committed via ConfigWriter (atomic 0600 + `.bak.<epoch>`). If validation fails, the original file is left untouched and the temp file is preserved so the operator can recover their edits
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config edit\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-editor\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the target config file in $EDITOR (default vi). On exit, the candidate is validated; on LGTM the file is committed via ConfigWriter (atomic 0600 + .bak.<epoch>). On validation failure the original is untouched and the temp file is preserved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR [default: policy]
Which file to open. Defaults to `policy`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
policy
.IP \(bu 2
authorized
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-editor\fR \fI<EDITOR>\fR
Override `$EDITOR`. Mostly for tests (e.g. `\-\-editor "cp my.toml"`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config edit
  $ rev\-stealth config edit \-\-target authorized
  $ EDITOR=nano rev\-stealth config edit

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Edit committed.
  1  UserError        Editor exit / candidate validation failure.
  3  PermanentError   ConfigWriter IO failure.

ENV:
  EDITOR                   Editor used (fallback: vi).
  REV_SCRAPING_POLICY      Override the policy.toml path.
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTHORIZED  Override the authorized.toml path.
